WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:07.480
&gt;&gt; All right. Hi
everyone, good afternoon.

00:00:07.481 --> 00:00:09.000
So, my name is
Phebe Vayanos and I'm

00:00:09.001 --> 00:00:11.430
Assistant Professor of
Industrial Engineering and

00:00:11.431 --> 00:00:12.720
Computer Science at USC

00:00:12.721 --> 00:00:14.100
and also Associate Director of

00:00:14.101 --> 00:00:16.515
the Center for AI
in Society at USC.

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:18.240
On behalf of my team,

00:00:18.241 --> 00:00:19.980
I would like to present
the problem that we have

00:00:19.981 --> 00:00:22.825
identified in the context
of AI and public health.

00:00:22.826 --> 00:00:26.980
It's the problem of
using AI to prevent VL.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:31.140
So, as Rishabh
presented yesterday,

00:00:31.141 --> 00:00:34.740
VL is a huge public
health problem.

00:00:34.741 --> 00:00:38.115
In fact, it's the second
largest parasitic killer

00:00:38.116 --> 00:00:41.795
in the entire world
after malaria.

00:00:41.796 --> 00:00:44.490
Every year there's about 200,000

00:00:44.491 --> 00:00:47.450
infections and
70% of those cases,

00:00:47.451 --> 00:00:49.645
actually of the cases
that occur in India,

00:00:49.646 --> 00:00:51.845
occur in Bihar and UP.

00:00:51.846 --> 00:00:55.800
There is a treatment that's
available for treating VL,

00:00:55.801 --> 00:00:59.285
but unfortunately it's
not widely available,

00:00:59.286 --> 00:01:01.830
it's not easily accessible.

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:06.860
The way that VL spreads
is actually by means of

00:01:06.861 --> 00:01:09.680
these sandflies which can

00:01:09.681 --> 00:01:12.985
carry the disease
and can infect you.

00:01:12.986 --> 00:01:17.075
There is a way of preventing VL,

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:21.660
which is by these indoor
residual spray approach.

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:26.300
This basically is a spray
that we go and place indoors

00:01:26.301 --> 00:01:30.440
inside houses and can
effectively eradicate the flies,

00:01:30.441 --> 00:01:32.965
and so prevent the spread
of the disease.

00:01:32.966 --> 00:01:36.760
The way this is performed
is basically twice yearly,

00:01:36.761 --> 00:01:40.060
before and after
the monsoon season.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.660
Unfortunately though, what
happens is that we need to

00:01:44.661 --> 00:01:48.325
have health workers that
actually go and do the spraying.

00:01:48.326 --> 00:01:52.330
A number of health workers
that we have at our disposal,

00:01:52.331 --> 00:01:54.110
amount of spray that we have at

00:01:54.111 --> 00:01:56.380
our disposal are both limited.

00:01:56.381 --> 00:01:58.490
Also the spring needs
to occur during

00:01:58.491 --> 00:02:00.395
a particular time
window in the year

00:02:00.396 --> 00:02:03.640
and so we have also
a time constraint.

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:08.535
AI can actually help
address this problem.

00:02:08.536 --> 00:02:12.040
In particular, the way in which
we can view this problem,

00:02:12.041 --> 00:02:14.650
what we need to do is we
have a finite number of

00:02:14.651 --> 00:02:16.810
health workers that can start at

00:02:16.811 --> 00:02:19.840
a particular village in India,

00:02:19.841 --> 00:02:22.150
and for each health worker,

00:02:22.151 --> 00:02:25.630
we can decide which cities
they will visit and the

00:02:25.631 --> 00:02:29.525
sequence in which they
will visit these villages.

00:02:29.526 --> 00:02:31.580
So this is a vehicle
routing problem.

00:02:31.581 --> 00:02:34.050
Whenever a public health worker

00:02:34.051 --> 00:02:35.850
visits a particular village,

00:02:35.851 --> 00:02:37.750
they can conduct
the spraying and we can

00:02:37.751 --> 00:02:40.500
decide the intensity
of the spraying.

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:42.220
Depending on the intensity,

00:02:42.221 --> 00:02:43.570
we will eradicate a certain

00:02:43.571 --> 00:02:45.040
proportion of the flies which in

00:02:45.041 --> 00:02:46.910
turn will prevent
a certain portion

00:02:46.911 --> 00:02:48.960
of the disease from spreading.

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:54.140
We have some data
already available at

00:02:54.141 --> 00:02:55.490
our disposal to help

00:02:55.491 --> 00:02:58.555
inform these decision
making problem.

00:02:58.556 --> 00:03:00.970
These are basically
patient-level data.

00:03:00.971 --> 00:03:06.890
So we have for both Bihar and UP
historical cases,

00:03:06.891 --> 00:03:10.250
so we can figure out when

00:03:10.251 --> 00:03:14.240
and where a particular
individual was affected by VL.

00:03:14.241 --> 00:03:16.640
I understand that
these people are also

00:03:16.641 --> 00:03:18.200
tracked in the system

00:03:18.201 --> 00:03:20.910
so we can know whether
they were cured.

00:03:20.911 --> 00:03:23.960
For each that we get,

00:03:23.961 --> 00:03:25.970
we also have
information about areas

00:03:25.971 --> 00:03:28.935
that were actually
sprayed in the past.

00:03:28.936 --> 00:03:31.480
We have a patient-level data,

00:03:31.481 --> 00:03:33.370
demographic
information and so on,

00:03:33.371 --> 00:03:37.675
and we also have elements
that can help that actually

00:03:37.676 --> 00:03:40.180
impact the efficacy
of the spraying

00:03:40.181 --> 00:03:42.980
such as cleanliness
of the households,

00:03:42.981 --> 00:03:45.520
the status of
the village et cetera.

00:03:45.521 --> 00:03:48.880
Apparently, if, say
your house is not so clean,

00:03:48.881 --> 00:03:52.730
then the efficacy of
the spraying will drop.

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:56.260
We believe that there
are some additional data

00:03:56.261 --> 00:03:57.460
that we could collect that could

00:03:57.461 --> 00:04:01.710
help inform our decision
making even better.

00:04:01.711 --> 00:04:04.630
In particular, deaths due to VL.

00:04:04.631 --> 00:04:06.460
So these would be cases
that have not been

00:04:06.461 --> 00:04:09.850
reported at the time
when they occur

00:04:09.851 --> 00:04:11.890
but that resulted in death.

00:04:11.891 --> 00:04:15.680
Also, additional data that
can help us understand maybe

00:04:15.681 --> 00:04:17.090
what other factors could

00:04:17.091 --> 00:04:19.340
affect the efficacy
of the spraying,

00:04:19.341 --> 00:04:22.670
like weather conditions
and things like that.

00:04:22.671 --> 00:04:25.190
What we propose to do is to take

00:04:25.191 --> 00:04:27.784
this historical data that
we have at our disposal,

00:04:27.785 --> 00:04:29.930
like historical cases of VL,

00:04:29.931 --> 00:04:31.490
whether the treatment
was successful,

00:04:31.491 --> 00:04:33.170
weather data et cetera,

00:04:33.171 --> 00:04:37.010
to train certain machine
learning models that will

00:04:37.011 --> 00:04:38.530
help us understand where will

00:04:38.531 --> 00:04:41.060
VL strike in the current year.

00:04:41.061 --> 00:04:44.960
That will help us also
understand the effectiveness and

00:04:44.961 --> 00:04:48.680
the efficacy of a particular
spraying strategy.

00:04:48.681 --> 00:04:52.275
We will use that information
then to inform,

00:04:52.276 --> 00:04:56.360
to feed into an optimization
model that would actually

00:04:56.361 --> 00:04:59.375
generate these routes for

00:04:59.376 --> 00:05:02.370
each and every of health worker.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:10.175
We believe that this approach
is very promising.

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:12.440
In particular, we believe that by

00:05:12.441 --> 00:05:14.960
using these data-driven
optimization approach,

00:05:14.961 --> 00:05:17.630
we'll be able to improve
both the efficacy and

00:05:17.631 --> 00:05:20.980
effectiveness of
these VL prevention strategy.

00:05:20.981 --> 00:05:22.640
We envisage

00:05:22.641 --> 00:05:27.000
some possible non-technical
roadblocks that we may face.

00:05:27.001 --> 00:05:29.570
In particular,
our proposed approach,

00:05:29.571 --> 00:05:30.979
because it will be implemented

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:33.370
actually by the government,

00:05:33.371 --> 00:05:35.750
it does require
government buy-in,

00:05:35.751 --> 00:05:38.120
but fortunately Rishabh does have

00:05:38.121 --> 00:05:40.700
contact with policymakers
in the area,

00:05:40.701 --> 00:05:43.175
so we're crossing our fingers.

00:05:43.176 --> 00:05:45.770
Some additional challenges relate

00:05:45.771 --> 00:05:48.220
to dropout rates of
these health workers.

00:05:48.221 --> 00:05:50.960
It seemed that every year
some of them dropped out,

00:05:50.961 --> 00:05:53.990
in which case you may need to
unexpected have to retrain

00:05:53.991 --> 00:05:57.020
health workers to teach

00:05:57.021 --> 00:05:59.080
them how they can
do the spraying.

00:05:59.081 --> 00:06:03.320
There are some ethical
concerns in particular.

00:06:03.321 --> 00:06:05.870
So we have these basically
scarce resources

00:06:05.871 --> 00:06:08.420
that we're seeking to
decide how to allocate.

00:06:08.421 --> 00:06:11.130
If we allocate them some place
and not somewhere else,

00:06:11.131 --> 00:06:12.380
we're effectively deciding who

00:06:12.381 --> 00:06:13.850
to treat and who
not to treat like

00:06:13.851 --> 00:06:17.545
who may get the disease
and who won't.

00:06:17.546 --> 00:06:19.890
This is very serious in my view.

00:06:19.891 --> 00:06:21.240
Ethical concern and how can

00:06:21.241 --> 00:06:26.295
we somehow tackle it
is maybe not clear.

00:06:26.296 --> 00:06:28.370
We have, of course,
privacy concerns

00:06:28.371 --> 00:06:30.185
related to the fact
that we will be using

00:06:30.186 --> 00:06:32.525
a patient-level data
and location like

00:06:32.526 --> 00:06:36.370
address information et cetera.

00:06:36.371 --> 00:06:38.800
The higher level, of course,

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:43.250
one can think about

00:06:43.251 --> 00:06:44.810
other health
priorities to address

00:06:44.811 --> 00:06:47.700
before this one and so.

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:51.755
Some concrete next steps.

00:06:51.756 --> 00:06:54.410
Some milestones
that we would like

00:06:54.411 --> 00:06:56.360
to reach in the
next year, I guess.

00:06:56.361 --> 00:06:58.670
We believe that we
can at least solve

00:06:58.671 --> 00:07:00.230
the technical parts of

00:07:00.231 --> 00:07:02.240
the project within
this coming year.

00:07:02.241 --> 00:07:04.670
First of all, we would
investigate whether

00:07:04.671 --> 00:07:06.740
these additional sources
of data that we

00:07:06.741 --> 00:07:09.965
believe would be helpful are
actually available to us.

00:07:09.966 --> 00:07:13.160
The second step
which we can start

00:07:13.161 --> 00:07:14.840
after the first few months of

00:07:14.841 --> 00:07:16.760
getting started with
the project would be actually

00:07:16.761 --> 00:07:19.805
this machine learning step
of doing these predictions,

00:07:19.806 --> 00:07:22.030
of predicting hotspots and

00:07:22.031 --> 00:07:24.235
effectiveness of
spraying et cetera.

00:07:24.236 --> 00:07:26.970
The last step would be actually
the optimizations step.

00:07:26.971 --> 00:07:28.070
I forgot to mention,

00:07:28.071 --> 00:07:31.070
this is actually
a relatively large scale problem

00:07:31.071 --> 00:07:33.200
because there's actually

00:07:33.201 --> 00:07:38.400
a thousand possible
villages where

00:07:38.401 --> 00:07:40.610
we could be spraying
giving rise to

00:07:40.611 --> 00:07:44.060
a huge number of possible routes
for the health workers,

00:07:44.061 --> 00:07:48.475
so we would have to do some work
on scalability at least.

00:07:48.476 --> 00:07:54.870
If successful, this AI
based prevention approach

00:07:54.871 --> 00:07:57.000
would be deployed
by the government.

00:07:57.001 --> 00:07:59.135
We don't think that
there is a need for a

00:07:59.136 --> 00:08:02.120
particularly fancy like
application to share the route.

00:08:02.121 --> 00:08:04.340
Instead, these can be
shared by just simply

00:08:04.341 --> 00:08:08.110
text message or
a paper-based transmissions.

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:12.230
We have identified two strategies

00:08:12.231 --> 00:08:15.560
for evaluating the impact
of our proposed approach.

00:08:15.561 --> 00:08:17.990
First of all, we can
go back and track

00:08:17.991 --> 00:08:20.690
now a decrease, hopefully,

00:08:20.691 --> 00:08:23.825
in the new cases of VL
for that given year,

00:08:23.826 --> 00:08:27.080
and then we can hopefully also

00:08:27.081 --> 00:08:28.335
showcase that maybe we we're

00:08:28.336 --> 00:08:30.200
able to increase the number of

00:08:30.201 --> 00:08:32.965
houses that actually
were sprayed.

00:08:32.966 --> 00:08:35.460
All right. This is it.

00:08:35.461 --> 00:08:38.380
Thank you very much for
your time and attention.

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:43.505
&gt;&gt; [inaudible] have one question.

00:08:43.506 --> 00:08:44.240
&gt;&gt; All right.

00:08:44.241 --> 00:08:46.115
&gt;&gt; So I was wondering,

00:08:46.116 --> 00:08:49.230
can you just train everyone to

00:08:49.231 --> 00:08:51.550
spray their own house?
Is it very hard?

00:08:51.551 --> 00:08:53.330
&gt;&gt; So, you would still
have I guess to get

00:08:53.331 --> 00:08:57.090
to them the product.

00:08:57.091 --> 00:08:59.110
So, even if they
knew how to spray,

00:08:59.111 --> 00:09:00.725
they'd need to have the tools

00:09:00.726 --> 00:09:02.670
and the chemicals
needed to spray.

00:09:02.671 --> 00:09:05.230
So you'd have a similar kind
of routing problem, right?

00:09:05.231 --> 00:09:07.870
You need to go and
to drop this off.

00:09:07.871 --> 00:09:12.345
But maybe actually, now
that I think about it,

00:09:12.346 --> 00:09:13.910
it's maybe a good idea
because you can

00:09:13.911 --> 00:09:15.650
always go and do it earlier.

00:09:15.651 --> 00:09:17.990
So now you don't have this
time constraint anymore.

00:09:17.991 --> 00:09:19.070
So also you may have-

00:09:19.071 --> 00:09:20.715
&gt;&gt; Make sure the drugs reach
everybody ahead of time.

00:09:20.716 --> 00:09:21.495
&gt;&gt; Right. You're right.

00:09:21.496 --> 00:09:23.400
&gt;&gt; Then you could train people.

00:09:23.401 --> 00:09:24.965
I don't know, maybe.
You know better.

00:09:24.966 --> 00:09:27.095
&gt;&gt; In the public health system,
you said they're not.

00:09:27.096 --> 00:09:32.795
Make sure that [inaudible]
have enough stocks.

00:09:32.796 --> 00:09:33.500
&gt;&gt; I see.

00:09:33.501 --> 00:09:38.040
&gt;&gt; They're [inaudible] the stocks
that [inaudible] before we start it.

00:09:38.041 --> 00:09:41.850
Okay, everyone is
spraying and it's not how

00:09:41.851 --> 00:09:47.880
much your product [inaudible].

00:09:47.881 --> 00:09:50.010
There's also another word
of mouth, right?

00:09:50.011 --> 00:09:53.370
You just leave it
to the [inaudible]

00:09:53.371 --> 00:09:54.585
As a public heath intervention,

00:09:54.586 --> 00:10:10.350
they will have to
introduce [inaudible].

00:10:10.351 --> 00:10:36.270
&gt;&gt; So that's actually
part of the [inaudible]

00:10:36.271 --> 00:10:39.305
&gt;&gt; I guess a while this
stops the time constraint,

00:10:39.306 --> 00:10:40.930
maybe you need more tools, right?

00:10:40.931 --> 00:10:42.920
You need the equipment
as well to spray,

00:10:42.921 --> 00:10:44.480
which would be more costly so,

00:10:44.481 --> 00:10:45.800
and we do have limitations in

00:10:45.801 --> 00:10:48.540
the amount of product
that's available as well.

